      "evidence": "**Evidence:**\n- **ICR is active and renewed**: OMB Control No. 2050-0144 was approved without change on **June 26, 2026** (Reginfo.gov), with expiration **June 30, 2029**. It was received by OIRA on September 30, 2025 (the prior expiration date), and OMB rules permit continued collection while renewal is pending.\n- **Collection is continuing**: RMP submission is statutorily mandated, and the Data Liberation Project's January 2026 FOIA release shows submissions through **December 31, 2025**, indicating ongoing collection and FOIA-based dissemination.\n- **Publication is delayed**: The RMP Public Data Tool has been **offline since April 2025** (over a year), and the agency says it is \"evaluating\" changes under the 2026 proposed rule with no fixed restoration date.\n- The 2026 proposed rule contemplates **retaining** a public data tool (in restricted form), so publication is delayed/redesigned rather than terminated.\n\n**Selected risk level: Moderate Risk.** The ICR is active (renewed before expiration) and collection continues, so this is not \"High Risk\" (no missed statutory deadline, no skipped collection, ICR not expired >1 year). But the **publication** channel has been offline since April 2025 with no firm return date \u2014 a clear publication delay.\n\n---"
